# Names tools/nsdns.py answers for a namespaced console, one per line.
# Re-read on every query, so editing this needs no restart and no root.
#
# The game looks up exactly these four (netrecon §70): the two WORMS.STUN
# names first -- and gives up with "Unable to connect to WormNet." without
# ever asking for the auth server if they come back NXDOMAIN -- then auth,
# then lsg. The generic stun.{us,eu,jp,au}.demonware.net strings in the binary
# are the bd SDK's compiled-in defaults, which the game empties and replaces
# with the WORMS pair before it starts networking; no console has ever queried
# them, so they are not listed and a query for one is logged as NXDOMAIN.
worms.stun.us.demonware.net
worms.stun.eu.demonware.net
worms-180.auth.mmp3.demonware.net
worms-180.lsg.mmp3.demonware.net
